Mon Jul 20 09:13:02 UTC 2026 - Michael Vetter <mvetter@suse.com>

- Update to 0.5.0:
  Breaking changes:
  * GTK 4.16 is now a requirement.
  * Removed the gtk4_8 feature, following the GTK 4.16 requirement.
  * Glycin is a new dependency.
  Features:
  * Add support for date/time localization under widget.clock.locale in the config.
  Bug fixes:
  * Fix high resource usage of GStreamer on static images by using glycin instead.
  * Fix momentary white flash/unthemed window on startup.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun May 31 01:04:22 UTC 2026 - Richard Rahl <rrahl0@opensuse.org>

- Update to version 0.4.0:
  + Config option to skip selecting user/session, with auto-login support and
    info message on skip. Passwordless users are excluded from auto-login
  + Added background image/webp/gif/video support via GStreamer
  + GTK4 pango markup is now supported in the clock widget format (the
    widget.clock.format configuration options)
  + The background_fit configuration option is now case-insensitive
  + greetd info messages are now displayed as notifications, just like greetd
    error messages
  + Session dropdown is not empty anymore on a fresh state file
  + Hid the border of the notification bar frame that shows up even when no
    notification is displayed

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Apr 11 22:24:30 UTC 2026 - Richard Rahl <rrahl0@opensuse.org>

- Update to version 0.3.0:
  + Users are now fetched from AccountsService instead of /etc/passwd. This
    provides better integration with modern desktop environments
  + GTK cursor blinking can now be disabled via the cursor_blink option

